    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Yeah, we're looking at using some simulation software, but it's hard to capture the more \"random\" stuff. It's like there are these tiny, sudden disruptions that don't follow a clear logic—just these weird, small interruptions that break the rhythm of the whole junction. Is there any way to categorize those specific types of small-scale, unpredictable disruptions that happen in an otherwise steady stream?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
