      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "These small-scale, unpredictable disruptions can often be categorized as localized microscopic instabilities within the traffic stream. They are sometimes referred to as \"phantom traffic jams\" or shockwave initiators, even if they are very brief. These events arise from poor driver reaction times interacting with capacity limits, rather than systemic design failure. Simulating these often requires incorporating more advanced, stochastic (random) driver models into your software.",
      "source": "target",
